                "source": [
                    "# Cash Fragmentation Analysis Fundamentals\n",
                    "## Overview\n",
                    "**Understanding and implementing cash fragmentation analysis for treasury optimization**\n",
                    "\n",
                    "## Introduction\n",
                    "This notebook provides comprehensive coverage of Cash Fragmentation Analysis techniques. It focuses on understanding how cash flows are distributed across different segments and how fragmentation impacts treasury management. The analysis helps treasury managers optimize liquidity, reduce transaction costs, and improve overall financial efficiency.\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Learning Objectives:\n",
                    "- Understand the concept of cash fragmentation and its impact on treasury operations\n",
                    "- Master techniques for identifying fragmentation patterns in treasury data\n",
                    "- Implement fragmentation analysis methodologies for optimization\n",
                    "- Develop strategies to consolidate fragmented cash flows\n",
                    "- Create visualization tools for fragmentation monitoring\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Prerequisites:\n",
                    "- Understanding of treasury operations and cash management\n",
                    "- Basic knowledge of financial data analysis\n",
                    "- Familiarity with Python for financial analysis\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Step-by-Step Instructions:\n",
                    "1. Load and preprocess treasury transaction data\n",
                    "2. Identify cash flow patterns and fragmentation indicators\n",
                    "3. Calculate fragmentation metrics and ratios\n",
                    "4. Visualize fragmentation patterns across time and segments\n",
                    "5. Develop optimization strategies for cash consolidation\n",
                    "6. Implement fragmentation monitoring dashboard\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Key Features:\n",
                    "- ✅ Fragmentation metrics calculation\n",
                    "- ✅ Interactive visualization of cash flow patterns\n",
                    "- ✅ Consolidation strategies generation\n",
                    "- ✅ Real-world treasury case studies\n",
                    "- ✅ Export capabilities for reporting\n",
                    "- ✅ Attribution support\n"
                ]
            },
            {
                "cell_type": "code",
                "execution_count": None,
                "metadata": {},
                "outputs": [],
                "source": [
                    "import pandas as pd\n",
                    "import numpy as np\n",
                    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                    "import seaborn as sns\n",
                    "\n",
                    "print('🚀 Treasury Analytics Notebook: Cash Fragmentation Analysis')\n",
                    "print('✅ Environment ready for treasury optimization analysis\n')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Generate synthetic treasury data for fragmentation analysis\n",
                    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
                    "\n",
                    "def generate_treasury_transactions(n_samples=1000):\n",
                    "    data = {\n",
                    "        'transaction_id': range(1, n_samples + 1),\n",
                    "        'amount': np.random.lognormal(8, 1.5, n_samples),\n",
                    "        'customer_segment': np.random.choice(['premium', 'standard', 'basic'], n_samples),\n",
                    "        'department': np.random.choice(['operations', 'finance', 'strategy'], n_samples),\n",
                    "        'transaction_type': np.random.choice(['payment', 'receipt', 'transfer', 'investment'], n_samples),\n",
                    "        'currency': np.random.choice(['USD', 'EUR', 'GBP', 'JPY'], n_samples),\n",
                    "        'timestamp': pd.date_range('2024-01-01', periods=n_samples, freq='H'),\n",
                    "        'is_critical': np.random.choice([True, False], n_samples, p=[0.1, 0.9]),\n",
                    "        'risk_score': np.random.beta(1, 3, n_samples)\n",
                    "    }\n",
                    "    return pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
                    "\n",
                    "df = generate_treasury_transactions(500)\n",
                    "\n",
                    "print('📊 Treasury Data Overview:')\n",
                    "print(f\"Total transactions: {len(df):,}\")\n",
                    "print(f\"Total volume: ₹{df['amount'].sum():,.0f}\")\n",
                    "print(f\"Unique customer segments: {df['customer_segment'].nunique()}\")\n",
                    "print(f\"Unique departments: {df['department'].nunique()}\")\n",
                    "print(f\"Date range: {df['timestamp'].min()} to {df['timestamp'].max()}\\n')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "print('🔍 Data Structure:')\n",
                    "print(df.head(3))\n"
                ]
            },
            {
                "cell_type": "code",
                "execution_count": None,
                "metadata": {},
                "outputs": [],
                "source": [
                    "# Cash Fragmentation Analysis Section\n",
                    "print('🔬 Cash Fragmentation Analysis:')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Fragmentation metrics calculation\n",
                    "print('💰 Fragmentation Metrics:')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Number of unique recipients (fragmentation indicator)\n",
                    "unique_recipients = df['customer_segment'].nunique()\n",
                    "print(f\"Number of customer segments (fragmentation): {unique_recipients}\")\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Transaction diversity index\n",
                    "unique_types = df['transaction_type'].nunique()\n",
                    "print(f\"Transaction types (diversity): {unique_types}\")\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Currency fragmentation\n",
                    "currency_fragmentation = df['currency'].nunique()\n",
                    "print(f\"Currencies involved (currency fragmentation): {currency_fragmentation}\")\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Department fragmentation (internal fragmentation)\n",
                    "department_fragmentation = df['department'].nunique()\n",
                    "print(f\"Departments processed (internal fragmentation): {department_fragmentation}\")\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Fragmentation score calculation (average of all fragmentation indicators)\n",
                    "fragmentation_score = (unique_recipients + unique_types + currency_fragmentation + department_fragmentation) / 4
",
                    "print(f\"Overall fragmentation score: {fragmentation_score:.2f} (1-10 scale)\")\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Risk score fragmentation (how risk is distributed)\n",
                    "risk_by_segment = df.groupby('customer_segment')['risk_score'].mean()
",
 "print('\nRisk Score by Segment:')
",
 "print(risk_by_segment)
",
 "# Currency-based fragmentation patterns\n",
 "print('\nCurrency-Based Fragmentation Patterns:')
",
 "currency_analysis = df.groupby('currency').agg({'amount': ['sum', 'count'], 'risk_score': 'mean'}).round(2)
",
 "print(currency_analysis)
",
 "# Temporal fragmentation (hourly patterns)\n",
 "print('\nTemporal Fragmentation Analysis:')
",
 "df['hour'] = df['timestamp'].dt.hour
",
 "hourly_volume = df.groupby('hour')['amount'].sum()\n",
 "print(f\"Peak hour: {hourly_volume.idxmax()} with volume: ₹{hourly_volume.max():,.0f}\")\n",
 "print(f\"Off-peak hours: {len(hourly_volume) - 1} hours with average volume: ₹{hourly_volume.mean():,.0f}\\n')\n",
 "print('🎯 Fragmentation Analysis Complete!')
"
                ]
            }
